    119, TODO, gpu, P1, "Finish macOS self-host deployment and GPU queue runtime verification; require reviewer approval before closing", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/mac_gpu_backend_evidence_2026-07-10.md, 1, , "2026-07-11 Metal readback/parity, host GPU queue, production wrapper, and MCP numeric/string ID handshake PASS. 2026-07-17 Apple Silicon Stage 3, Chrome/Electron Metal backing, fresh current MCP/LSP native protocol, and normal-scene current host-GPU parity PASS. The GPU-only zero-length readback root is the disjoint Rust-runtime/Simple-core array registry: Simple-core now owns rt_u32s_from_raw, its archive exports the symbol, and a strict no-stub native ABI probe preserves three exact u32 words with length 3. Metal submission ownership now separates all five known-uncommitted cleanup paths from committed-but-unknown quarantine. The full 1024-pixel clip scene still requires a fresh capped run. The live gate selects a real Simple Web/winit host and requires keyboard, explicit pointer movement, completed primary-button titlebar/body control clicks, and completion-only screenshot pixels; press/non-primary releases fail closed, the pure policy passes 6/6, and the source gate passes 7/7, while executable window proof remains open. Full deployment, live-window PASS, Intel-host, Metal clip, and reviewer gates remain open under TODO 531.", open, true
