    535, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Compose an exact-entry Stage 4 full-CLI host-provider profile from ABI-disjoint component archives without reopening hosted runtime bundles for applications.", src/app/cli/main.spl, 1, , "Linux exact provider composition and the 73-hook compiler backfill are complete. macOS physical-source closure and import resolution are bounded; a phase-profiled exact-entry run reached native linking, and canonical module identifiers no longer leak absolute workspace paths into generated C symbols. A clean 708-unit Stage3 rebuild passed sanity, and its focused Stage4 path reached the ordinary unresolved-provider link set. Provider object selection now requires exact or underscore-delimited runtime_<provider> identity across Unix/MSVC/MinGW shapes, while exact ABI scanning remains the content owner. The canonical bootstrap wrapper still re-entered the pre-object whole-tree path and was stopped at 5.8 GiB RSS after 3m42s on the third bounded cycle, so executable Stage4 proof remains open. TODO 579 owns the next source-matched Stage3 rebuild and honest SMF proof before any fresh capped Stage4 cycle. FreeBSD/Windows provider preparation remains open.", open, true
