    559, TODO, compiler, P1, "Preserve Optional not-found semantics when bootstrap MIR lowers rfind on an erased text receiver.", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/path.spl, 23, , "2026-08-18 RESOLVED as a stdlib contract bug, not a MIR lowering bug. rfind/find/index_of are RAW i64 sentinel APIs (-1 = miss) by design; the interpreter deliberately removed Optional treatment because index 3 aliases the nil sentinel. A repo-wide audit found exactly 6 offending sites, all three copies of std.path (nogc_sync_mut/path.spl:23,37; gc_async_mut/path.spl:23,37; nogc_async_mut_noalloc/path/baremetal_path.spl:54,71), which matched Some/nil on the sentinel so the Some arm always won binding idx=-1. Every OTHER stdlib consumer already tested < 0 correctly. RED: dirname(\"foo.txt\")=\"\" extension(\"README\")=\"README\" stem(\"README\")=\"\". Fixed by replacing the Optional match with an explicit sentinel test. GREEN 4/4 on test/01_unit/lib/path/path_rfind_sentinel_not_found_spec.spl (proven RED 1/4 with the fix stashed) and 4/4 on test/01_unit/lib/path/text_search_sentinel_contract_spec.spl. No MIR lowering change was needed or made.", done, true
    560, TODO, compiler, P1, "Replace the focused Stage4 compiler capsule's direct rt_cranelift ABI with a typed compiler-provider surface.", src/compiler_rust/compiler_backfill/src/lib.rs, 1, , "the focused bridge derives its exact 73-hook contract from the runtime-isolated crate, matches both canonical Simple facades, localizes non-contract definitions, rejects provider overlap and runtime dependencies, and uses a raw pointer/length object-emission ABI; remove the direct rt_ surface and prove cross-target x86_64/aarch64/riscv64 parity before widening its use", open, true
    561, TODO, compiler, P1, "Allow a binary operator at end of line to continue its right-hand expression at the current indentation level in the pure-Simple parser.", src/compiler/10.frontend/core/tokens.spl, 519, , "shared token_requires_rhs now drives both CoreLexer and the legacy scanner without consuming structural INDENT/DEDENT; 2026-08-18: focused regression landed at test/01_unit/compiler/parser_trailing_operator_continuation_spec.spl (b30437727b1) covering +/-/*//%, and/or, ==/<, bitwise |/&, a four-line chain, precedence across folds, return/reassign/if-condition positions and two NEGATIVE controls; every body executed correctly via direct bin/simple run, so the SEED parser has no defect here. Row stays open because that probe exercises the Rust seed, not the pure-Simple parser this row names; the bin/simple test harness verdict is also still deferred. same-indent bitwise-OR regression added, but its focused run is blocked because the canonical release binary identifies as the Rust seed and aborts on unknown extern rt_cli_arg_count; verify after pure-Simple deployment before closing 2026-08-18 PREMISE CORRECTION: the stated blocker is no longer true. The focused run is NOT blocked -- bin/simple test on that spec completes and reports Results: 8 total, 8 passed, 0 failed (exit 0), with no rt_cli_arg_count abort. Row stays open ONLY for the remaining honest reason: that harness run still executes the Rust seed, so it does not yet exercise the pure-Simple parser this row names; re-verify after pure-Simple deployment before closing.", open, true
    562, TODO, compiler, P1, "Include resolved import/provider ownership and dependency source hashes in native object-cache invalidation.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/native_project/mod.rs, 1243, , "current keys hash only the local module plus build context/compiler executable, while pure-Simple BuildCache stores empty dependencies. GPU daemon evidence: changing daemon_runner rebuilt 2 modules but retained older flattened simpleos_gpu_host__main___process_request objects; touching main rebuilt only spl_main. A fresh 217-module cache independently reproduced the 8x value, so cache invalidation is real but no longer the value-path blocker", open, true
    563, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Capture QEMU max RSS and warm multi-sample render/readback latency so NFR-003 and NFR-005 use measured p95 and combined QEMU-plus-daemon memory rather than daemon-only metadata.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-qemu-host-gpu-2d.shs, 1, , "the source/parser/cached-validator/self-test contract now requires 20 post-oracle warm receipts and nearest-rank p95 bound to exact matching-native QEMU accelerator argv, while RSS sampling carries daemon/QEMU/combined maxima across AArch64 boots. Each run now binds readiness to a fresh daemon instance and rejects daemon exit during or at QEMU completion; the bounded metrics lifetime self-test passes. Fresh current-host native/TCG execution and combined RSS remain open, TCG is correctness-only, and the default timeout stays unchanged unless real evidence requires a per-run override", open, true
