    572, TODO, compiler, P1, "Execute focused SSpec files through a result-bearing pure-Simple compiler/test-runner path without rt_cli_run_tests, the Rust rt_cli_run_file interpreter, SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_DRIVER, or a seed subprocess.", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/test_runner/test_runner_execute.spl, 54, , "the current CLI test arm calls rt_cli_run_tests and the pure-Simple orchestrator still executes specs through the Rust rt_cli_run_file path; wire driver_api_interpret to a BDD pass/fail result, consume it in run_test_file_interpreter, route the CLI to the pure-Simple runner, and prove one passing plus one failing no-seed spec; separate from TODO 548 host-GPU candidate admission", open, true
    573, TODO, runtime, P1, "Provide provider-complete timeout/capture, process-tree cleanup, child-scoped environment, and atomic unique-temp facades; remove POSIX env/mktemp admission dependencies.", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/io/process_ops.spl, 1, , "all five split _QemuRunner modules use shared owners; process_ops still uses GNU timeout on Unix and cmd /c plus temp files on Windows; the Rust SFFI rt_process_run_timeout preserves argv but core-C lacks the provider, its timeout child omits Unix process-group setup before group kill, Windows lacks Job Object cleanup, timeout_ms<=0 semantics differ, and no native child-env overlay or host unique-temp API exists; implement provider parity and argv/stdout/stderr/deadline/orphan tests before runner env/mktemp removal", open, true
    574, TODO, runtime, P1, "Provide overflow-safe cross-platform monotonic millisecond conversion and split QEMU runner elapsed timing from wall-clock artifact stamps.", src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/io/time_ops.spl, 49, , "runner_targets _now_ms preserves Unix wall-clock behavior through current_time_ms for serial filenames and build markers while elapsed timing still shares that clock; audit and align platform_win.h plus runtime_time.c QPC multiply-before-divide overflow, native_all rt_time_now_monotonic_ms using SystemTime wall clock, and simple_core core_process.spl Linux-specific CLOCK_MONOTONIC id/layout before closing", open, true
    575, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Prove or reject direct SimpleOS guest Vulkan/CUDA access through QEMU passthrough independently of the ivshmem host-daemon offload path.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-qemu-guest-gpu-passthrough.shs, 1, , "read-only self-test/preflight now verifies trusted system QEMU identity/device help, complete IOMMU-group VFIO ownership, and explicit approval, while deliberately refusing caller-authored guest receipts until a canonical SimpleOS guest producer exists. The 2026-07-15 host remains unavailable: both NVIDIA GPUs are host-bound, virtio-gpu-gl has an unresolved qemu_egl_display symbol, and SimpleOS has no guest Vulkan/CUDA producer. Never rebind a live device without explicit maintenance approval; ivshmem remains a separate supported path", open, true
    576, TODO, engine2d, P1, "Provide a host-daemon Engine2D module/runtime boundary compatible with the tagged Rust RuntimeValue ABI without retaining unrelated optional backend symbols.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/native_project/linker.rs, 478, , "ordinary object relocations no longer become forced runtime roots; live strong references extract archive members, explicit lifecycle/fallback roots remain, and the weak security loader is conditional. Focused section-GC/security tests pass and the 208-module tagged Vulkan/CUDA daemon links without core-C ABI mixing or generated stubs", done, false
    577, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Make the linked native host-GPU daemon enter the ivshmem service loop and advance HELLO generation before guest negotiation.", src/app/simpleos_gpu_host/main.spl, 1, , "2026-07-15 bounded AArch64 TCG run maps ivshmem and records RSS but reports attempts=0, first/final generation=0, software fallback reason 7; daemon logs only HOST_GPU_DAEMON_SELECTOR. Trace startup/runtime initialization and retain one correlated Vulkan/CUDA receipt without rerunning bootstrap", open, true
    578, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Provide one duplicate-free x86 minimal freestanding runtime owner for the host-GPU probe without relying on linker multiple-definition ordering.", examples/09_embedded/simple_os/arch/x86_64/boot/rt_extras.c, 1, , "the rejected diagnostic whole-file admission overlaps strong rt_tuple_new/get/set/len and rt_rdrand definitions with baremetal_stubs.c; -z muldefs masks nondeterministic ownership. Extract the required core contracts or remove duplicate owners, then rebuild once with function/data sections and exact symbol-owner checks", open, true
    579, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Verify labeled tuple return parsing and the honest Stage3 SMF compile command in a fresh bounded bootstrap cycle.", src/compiler/10.frontend/core/parser.spl, 1, , "current source parses label: Type tuple elements while retaining their element types; a focused direct-parser regression passes 3/3 for the canonical process result, mixed labeled/anonymous elements, and malformed missing types. Bootstrap compile deletes stale output and rejects missing or <=300-byte artifacts. A post-rebase source-spec launch exposed and fixed the final reserved function binding in MIR module lowering; literal shell interpolation braces were also corrected, and the Stage4 source contract now guards all three lowering files with 14/14 passing. The prior rebuild session reached its three-cycle cap; rebuild with SIMPLE_NO_STUB_FALLBACK=1, run an exact print-SMF oracle, then feed the verified artifact into the macOS live-window gate", open, true
    580, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Deploy a source-matched pure-Simple CLI, then unblock fresh CUDA, Vulkan, and Metal evidence.", src/app/io/_CliCompile/compile_targets.spl, 633, , "2026-07-26 CUDA live submit/readback passes on both NVIDIA devices with stable generated PTX and zero fill/copy/alpha/scroll mismatches. Cached-native Metal source emission passes with four hash markers; live Metal remains a macOS-host row. Vulkan provider retention is implemented and its linker regression passes 13/13; retained hardware reaches Initialized, strict creation, and backend_name=vulkan. The next crash is a cross-module Engine2DReadback field-layout mismatch: producer pixels offset 0, caller offset 0x50 from a colliding module-local SymbolId. MIR now prescans callable return shapes by exact symbol name, uses module-qualified aggregate layout aliases, validates static-vs-instance imported method fallback, and prevents legacy unresolved metadata from overwriting canonical provenance. The final layout source contract passes 2/2. The Dict/DiContainer same-name dispatch defect is repaired in source and its contract passes 3/3; three retained-cache builds completed at 6 compiled/729 cached, 3/732, and 4/731, with no bootstrap or cache reset. The resulting driver no longer segfaults and reaches phase 3, but the two-file oracle completes analysis then logs no mode matched, exits zero, and emits no binary because CompileMode is corrupted before phase dispatch. Post-return mode reassignment and discriminant dispatch were ineffective and removed. The new executable same-name regression remains blocked behind that transport defect. The three-cycle cap is reached. The default ProcessingIR daemon now validates FillU32 device output without allocating and executing a duplicate CPU result; CPU execution is lazy for fallback and explicit under --processing-verify-cpu for parity/performance evidence. Unit 3/3, fallback policy 9/9 before its strengthened duplicate-call assertion, reason mapping 6/6, and daemon check pass; the corrected final policy assertion and fresh source-matched latency medians remain open under the cycle cap. The hosted response-route, process/pipe, and compositor revision-cache perf specs now cover the full request/reply path plus strict software, CUDA, Vulkan, and Metal cache rows. Fresh cached-interpreter diagnostics are recorded in doc/09_report/hosted_compositor_revision_cache_measurement_2026-07-30.md: software passes at 4,111,102,510/4,266,039 ns forced/hit p50; CUDA smoke fails at 6,466,705,755/7,273,005,377 ns with device_identity_unknown, handle 0, and nil identity; Vulkan fails on missing rt_is_interpreter_runtime. The process/pipe parser now clears the production process module after grouping its redirect condition, then fails in browser_session.spl; split assignments and its first ungrouped header condition are normalized, but the third capped run still reports a newline parse error and executes zero examples. Worker response-route and process/pipe execution remain unaccepted. These are not accepted source-matched evidence. This is now the critical P1 pure-Simple WM -> GUI/Web -> DrawIrComposition -> Engine2D lane. Resume on prepared hosts with a clean revision, admitted pure-Simple compiler, immutable runtime/provider provenance, a direct native CompileMode transport regression, the typed-instance plus imported-static oracle returning 84, static pixels-offset verification, CPU-SIMD oracle, Vulkan/Metal device-origin readback, identical scene/event traces, x86/ARM QEMU receipts, and one readback/handle/identity/checksum/parity cycle. Electron is noncritical and postponed under TODO 583. See doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/wm_glass_theme_host_simpleos.md, doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/simpleos_qemu_host_gpu_external_host_evidence.md, and doc/08_tracking/bug/native_engine2d_readback_cross_module_field_layout_2026-07-26.md.", open, true
    581, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Restore current-main Linux Stage2/Stage3 dynload bootstrap after LLVM virtual dispatch reaches the final link.", doc/08_tracking/bug/seed_stage2_llvm_method_symbol_lowering_2026-07-17.md, 1, , "2026-07-25 clean-cache Stage2 and Stage3 dynload bootstrap passed compiler sanity after canonical PTX float bits, ELF relocation mapping, and rt_dict_set lowering fixes", done, false
    582, TODO, compiler, P1, "Attach module-export owner metadata to the exact fresh-load dictionary returned by the Rust interpreter loader.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/interpreter_module/module_loader.rs, 1049, , "The fresh full-module path now returns the exact cached exports_value, grouped aliased imports are installed with source provenance, and the focused owner/global regression binary passes 15/15 including the new unflattened transitive growing-global alias case.", done, false
    583, TODO, gui, P3, "Run the optional Electron Aetheric rendering, interaction, and capture proof after the critical pure WM/GUI/Web/Engine2D line.", doc/09_report/aetheric_host_web_gui_readiness_2026-07-26.md, 1, , "POSTPONED by user direction on 2026-07-26. Strict worktree-local Electron 42.5.0 resolution and Aetheric identity admission are integrated, but no compiler/provider input was admitted, no Electron process was launched, and no live proof exists. Resume only after TODO 580's pure-Simple CPU-SIMD/Vulkan/Metal and x86/ARM QEMU plan reaches an appropriate checkpoint and the user reactivates this lane. Do not use npx/PATH/global fallback. Postponement is not completion.", open, true
    584, TODO, compiler, P1, "Repair native OptimizationPipeline aggregate transport before resuming the 84 oracle and Vulkan readback.", src/compiler/60.mir_opt/mir_opt/mod.spl, 748, , "The crashing backend builders now mutate a fresh optimizationpipeline_for_level result instead of returning a newly constructed aggregate; the focused transport source regression passes. The 73 and 84 gates now require the same hash-bound non-seed producer, compiler backfill, and runtime archive; both source contracts pass, and 84 no longer invokes literal bin/simple. One cache-preserving no-opt, no-stub incremental build reached LLVM entry-closure diagnostics but timed out after 900 seconds with no artifact; retained log: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/commit-6848f3cc1e21-build.log. Produce the source-matched compiler without bootstrap or cache reset, then execute exact outputs 73 and 84 before resuming Vulkan device readback.", open, true
    585, TODO, runtime, P1, "Provide an admitted no-stub runtime lane for the pure-Simple compiler entry closure.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/native_project/config.rs, 3159, , "The guarded native_build_worker accepts standard native-build argv, and the hash-bound 73/84 gates enable worker mode. Root source repairs include the exact core-C plus dedicated compiler-backfill Stage4 authorization, HmInferContext.accumulate_effect, TraitSolver.find_trait_for_method, direct owner imports, and one-argument ObligationCause.MethodCall; the focused Rust authorization test passes 1/1. On 2026-07-28 the duplicate-owner root was repaired: body-bearing runtime/builtin/import-like functions retain module ownership, LLVM resolves only declarations through imports, and the hardened object fingerprint now includes compiler-producer identity. The focused ownership regression passes 1/1. LLVM release seed 9852ccffdf78c4e5fbbb902c62c83e3b9a678d323ebab5d8b9a24d3041ef589d rebuilt without bootstrap; the worker then rebuilt 683/683 for producer invalidation and linked with zero failures. A traced one-file probe proved AOT dispatch and localized the first crash to backend LLVM capability discovery: backend_shell_tuple built a mixed text/list aggregate immediately before process_run. The shared helper now calls process_run directly in each OS branch, and gate 73 pins that source contract. On 2026-07-28 the exact authorized native_build_worker.spl entry rebuilt incrementally at 3 compiled/680 cached, zero failed, hash e41c69b275cdd0e79e4ccadbb79e562bc7aa50d1c0da8b8b552c589e2a64617e. Native GDB probes then found two representation defects in the shared closure scanner: optional find positions were compared as tagged integers, and text.bytes array values divisible by eight were decoded as tagged integers. The scanner now uses a portable contains-guarded text index helper plus raw char_code_at validation, and skips triple-quote splitting on ordinary lines. An intermediate 4-compiled/679-cached worker da97dfc9da8a06f42eec36dfc686f14f6173e9fc970f02cbbb0aab926b6a9214 returned both compiler.driver.driver and compiler.common.driver_core_types from the real entry; the interpreter probe produced all seven expected import/sibling vectors. Gate 73 moved past unresolved symbols but its outer runner timed out while the closure child stayed at 99 percent CPU, reached about 16 GB RSS, and emitted no driver before its 600-second bound. A compilation-free direct closure probe independently reached about 4.8 GB RSS in 40 seconds and was stopped after two minutes. The final contains-guarded helper is intentionally unrerun after the three-cycle cap. Next session: incrementally rebuild only the changed worker units, run one explicitly time/RSS-bounded closure trace, and rerun gate 73 only if discovery converges inside the smoke budget; gate 84 remains unrun. The direct-owner trait fixture remains nil. Do not reset cache, run full bootstrap, or use hosted/all fallback.", open, true
    586, TODO, gpu, P1, "Measure the source-matched ProcessingIR production daemon after removing duplicate CPU work.", src/app/simpleos_gpu_host/daemon_runner.spl, 292, , "PASS: clean CUDA/Vulkan/runtime-symbol-table archive c2f59287329e92d617d2900c360ae3448190af9bcb5bd86dbb6e215f33429bfd produced source-matched host-gpu daemon 0024604345d7641912d5ad1d53f93aef9565db120fdd4f4cf18f523400607c96. device-warm-production passed three warmups plus five measured 1048576-element CUDA requests with verifier disabled, zero HOST_GPU_PROCESS_PERF records, exact checksum 809508928, handle 1, stable identity 1002905313239842438, and medians 218205 us device, 318606 us round trip, 100401 us non-device overhead. TODO 587 owns the observed latency regression.", done, false
    587, TODO, gpu, P1, "Explain and reduce the source-matched CUDA device and round-trip median regression.", src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/sffi/file_io/file_ops.rs, 1020, , "PASS: the unpinned 218205/318606 us run was host-load-sensitive. With both artifacts pinned to CPUs 28-31, baseline medians are 119311 us device, 171572 us round trip, and 52261 us non-device. Commit b658e408064a replaces 1048576 exported rt_array_push calls plus 1048576 exported rt_array_get calls with checked direct RuntimeArray slice loops while preserving packed-array fallback. Runtime 3d24c72e59735791941983517cc222ff5fc9a4112b668ef098dbfa4ceab244c0 and daemon 2f502746885a73e81e675405cca62a3c75e5f0e00795e49926093cff206d452e pass the same exact production gate at 88569/93250/4507 us, reductions of 25.8/45.6/91.4 percent, with stable CUDA provenance and zero CPU comparison records. Strict Vulkan probe fd9fa68a06ac4eb32182eab5bcc19095aaed89ceb8220078c89e229e045bdd4d against the same runtime passes exact output, all five typed failures, and same-process recovery with stable identity 666008366.", done, false
    588, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run and admit prepared-macOS Metal and Vulkan GPU processing/readback evidence with exact pixels, stable device identity, and zero CPU fallback.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/gpu_backend_mac_host_remaining.md, 12, , "The host-neutral backend_metal_mac_host_resume_contract_spec now has six examples and 99 source-contract assertion sites covering every prepared-host path plus generated Metal create/pipeline/dispatch/commit/wait/download, exact checksums and mismatch gates, framebuffer device origin, CPU parity, positive handle/identity, no fallback, and 21-pair Metal/Vulkan cache timing. These checks prove source presence, not execution. The macOS preparation lane now requires the canonical Metal trusted-build manifest admission, binds the generated receipt to its admitted Simple binary plus canonical generated MSL source and metallib path/hash records, rejects caller path overrides that do not match admission, and requires a zero harness exit before gpu-readback-verified with nonzero equal checksums and zero mismatches. It also records stable initial/Draw IR/interaction Metal device identity. The admitted windowless MSL micro diagnostic is documented as library-creation preflight only. No macOS host PASS is claimed. On a prepared macOS host with an accepted self-hosted binary, run the host-neutral contract plus test/03_system/gpu/metal_backend_mac_host_spec.spl, test/03_system/check/macos_vulkan_processing_ir_live_readback_parity_spec.spl, and test/05_perf/web_render_chrome/web_draw_ir_gpu_route_device_measured_spec.spl using the exact commands in the linked plan. Keep open until the contract passes 6/6 and fresh receipts prove generated Metal submit/readback, nonzero fill/copy/alpha/scroll checksums, exact Metal framebuffer pixels, primary Draw IR route calibration/reuse, 21-pair hosted compositor Metal/Vulkan revision-cache timing with device provenance and hit p50 at least five percent below forced-render p50, Vulkan ProcessingIR 64-value exact parity, positive stable device identity/handle, max channel delta zero, failure-injection receipts, and no CPU mirror or fallback.", open, true
    589, TODO, compiler, P1, "Finish the bounded pure-Simple compiler entry closure after duplicate discovery was removed.", src/app/io/_CliCompile/compile_targets.spl, 1073, , "2026-07-28: native Dict membership admitted duplicate closure paths, reaching 19,625 visited and 73,890 queued in 60 seconds. Reusing the existing exact text bucket set converges; pub-use scanning and importer-relative bare-module resolution yield 448 files. Reachable driver error, registry, native-lib, and null-block sources now use canonical case syntax; the internal null status value no longer claims an unused packed ABI. The broad HIR unresolved cascade was first hidden by the light daemon dropping the requested timeout at its direct-child handoff. The daemon now forwards its remaining deadline and the focused bounded-runner contract passes 14/14. Hash-bound Gate 73 then ran for 242 seconds instead of dying at 120 seconds, but failed deterministically during HIR import/global registration with unresolved compiler_driver_create, CompileMode, CompileContext, HmInferContext, validate_value_struct_layouts, and many sibling symbols; no exact 73 binary exists. The phase-2 logical module map now uses the repository's compiled-safe persistent Dict set operation, and its focused source regression passes 1/1. Producer diagnosis is now exact: native_build_worker-current and find-fix discover only one source and fail/crash in native_build_entry_args; bucket-discovery and later pre-handoff workers discover 425-455 sources but skip logical registration and reproduce the HIR cascade; alias-handoff discovers the closure but embeds the old indexed module-map update. An essential cache-preserving Rust-seed worker rebuild was attempted only to break this self-hosting cycle, without a full bootstrap or cache reset, but hit its explicit 600-second worker bound and produced no artifact; the existing cache manifest was unchanged. A cache-preserving Rust release seed rebuild restored JIT lowering for panic through canonical rt_panic. Subsequent bounded probes advanced through mutable VHDL planning, the whole-closure ConstValue owner collision, and the stale six-argument specialized-template callers. Both callers now use compile_specialized_template_default and the focused source contract passes 1/1. The Rust JIT flattener now retries the owner module path for direct symbol imports and flattens symbols from non-package source files; its focused regression passes 1/1. Incremental seed 513c1792712fd10bf080f66b695b0c18f1a468662a4db45382a3b5b6dceebca5 was built without bootstrap or cache reset. The next probe passed that blocker and stopped at enum SymbolType missing variant Type. Writer-local SmfSymbol/SymbolBinding/SymbolType were renamed to distinct SmfWriter owners and their source contract passes 1/1, but the third probe proves src/compiler/99.loader/module_loader.spl still contributes a two-variant SymbolType collision. No replacement worker was emitted; retained logs are direct-symbol-jit-build-6.log and writer-symbol-jit-build-7.log, and the worker cache remains intact. Next session: rename the loader-local SymbolType and its facade export, then run one cache-preserving worker probe. Do not rerun Gate 73 until a replacement worker exists. Gate 84 remains unrun under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    590, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue TODO 589 after loader symbol ownership and helper typing repairs.", src/compiler/99.loader/jit_instantiator.spl, 147, , "LoaderSymbolType now owns the compatibility loader's Function/Data model and explicitly converts linker SmfObjectSymbolType; focused symbol ownership contract passes 1/1. Shared loaded-metadata helpers now use Dict<text, LoadedMetadata>, and generic unload ownership helpers use Dict<text, (text, T)>; focused helper contract passes 1/1. Three bounded retained-cache probes cleared those blockers and now stop at untyped rec_cache in _jit_cache_owner. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/loader-symbol-jit-build-8.log, loader-metadata-jit-build-9.log, unload-owner-jit-build-10.log. The compatibility JitInstantiator still declares bare jit_cache: Dict while storing code/address/owner records. Next session: type jit_cache and both rec_cache helpers with the smallest explicit dynamic record contract, then run one cache-preserving worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    591, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue TODO 590 after typed compatibility JIT cache and mutating loader wrappers.", src/compiler/90.tools/fix/rules/impl_/lint_short_grammar.spl, 3, , "JitCacheRecord now owns code/address/owner, jit_cache is Dict<text, JitCacheRecord>, and all consumers use typed fields; the focused helper contract passes 1/1. Loader SMF conversion now imports canonical SymbolType without a flattened type alias. Mutating moduleloader wrappers use me while read-only wrappers remain fn; focused contracts pass 1/1. Three bounded retained-cache probes cleared those blockers and now stop at Unknown variable compiler_fix_text_index_len while lowering check_short_grammar_refactor. The file already imports helpers.* plus {_text_index_len as compiler_fix_text_index_len}; this is the same flattened function-alias loss pattern. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/jit-cache-record-build-11.log, canonical-symbol-type-build-12.log, loader-mutability-build-13.log. Next session: import/call canonical _text_index_len directly with one source regression, then run one cache-preserving worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    592, TODO, compiler, P1, "Resolve lint-short-grammar helper ownership after flattened alias removal.", src/compiler/90.tools/fix/rules/impl_/lint_short_grammar.spl, 2, , "TODO 591's aliased helper was replaced first by an explicit private import, then a public text_index_len import, then the existing single helpers.* edge. All three focused cycles fail in the test-runner child with semantic variable text_index_len not found, proving the nested flattened helpers module is not exposing this function; no worker probe was run this session after the focused cap. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/lint-short-grammar-helper-contract.log through lint-short-grammar-helper-contract-3.log. The new source contract intentionally remains failing as executable evidence. Next session: either localize the five-line character counter in lint_short_grammar.spl or repair nested-glob flattening with a minimal Rust fixture, then make the focused contract pass before any worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588. RESOLVED 2026-08-18 via the localize option. Ownership: lint_short_grammar.spl:33-37 owns its own five-line counter _lint_text_index_len (called at :30); helpers.spl:145 keeps its private _text_index_len for its own callers (:38,:70,:83,:84). Underscore-private names cannot cross a glob re-export, so no import edge can ever expose it -- the localized copy is the only single-owner answer, and the helpers.* glob at :3 stays because LineContext and replace_interpolation_identifier still come through it. Contract spec now GREEN: Results: 1 total, 1 passed, 0 failed. Positive control: check_short_grammar_refactor on 'items.map(\\x: x.trim())' yields 1 finding (method reference &:trim); negative control on 'items.map(&:trim)' yields 0. Rule stays wired at registry.spl:56,154.", done, true
    593, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after strict shared-binding repairs.", src/compiler/20.hir/hir_types.spl, 348, , "The lint short-grammar counter is now local and its focused source contract passes 1/1. Draw IR SDN serialization now joins immutable segments, preserving the existing wire format; its direct Rust-seed JIT check has no JIT or memory-safety error, while the broad behavior spec could not execute examples because the unrelated test-runner closure still fails on legacy syntax. MethodResolution.get_symbol_id now returns directly from its match, and interpreter AOP collection mutates a val array. Three retained-cache worker cycles cleared out:163 and the final cycle deterministically reached mutable shared binding found:348 in SymbolTable.get_symbol_raw before timing out during interpreter fallback. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/draw-ir-strict-build-15.log and shared-binding-build-16.log. Next session: replace get_symbol_raw's optional accumulator with a direct guarded return, run one focused contract, then one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    594, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after HIR symbol lookup and rename copy-on-write repairs.", src/compiler/20.hir/hir_types.spl, 448, , "SymbolTable.get_symbol_raw now returns directly from its has guard. SymbolTable.rename_symbol now reconstructs the shared HirSymbol with every field copied and only name replaced, satisfying strict copy-on-write lowering. The focused HIR shared-binding source contract passes 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared found:348, refined renamed:388 to a W1001 shared-field mutation, then cleared that path and reached mutable shared binding owner_module:448 in method_symbol_name. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/symbol-lookup-build-17.log, symbol-rename-build-18.log, and symbol-cow-build-19.log. Next session: normalize owner_module without a mutable text binding, extend the focused contract, and run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    595, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after immutable HIR owner paths, MIR call destinations, and statement optionals.", src/compiler/20.hir/hir_lowering/expressions.spl, 316, , "method_symbol_name now uses a private value-returning owner-module normalizer; its source contract passes 1/1 and behavior spec passes 2/2 including repeated parent prefixes and source-path qualification. Direct and indirect MIR call emitters now construct flat optional destinations with conditional val expressions; focused contract passes 1/1. Tuple-destructure and return lowering now use val arrays plus direct match/conditional optionals; focused contract passes 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared owner_module:448, dest:413 and its indirect sibling, then reached fld_module_base_sym:316. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/owner-module-build-20.log, call-dest-build-21.log, and hir-statement-build-22.log. Next session: replace the expressions.spl optional accumulators at lines 316, 329, 370, 399, 428, and 937 with direct match/value or value-returning search patterns, add one focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    596, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after HIR expression and module optional-binding repairs.", src/compiler/20.hir/hir_lowering/_Items/module_lowering.spl, 770, , "Field lowering now uses value-returning symbol extraction, reverse last-match module callable lookup, tuple element lookup, and local/declared/self field type resolution. Every remaining mutable optional in expressions.spl was replaced by match values or a recursive left fold that preserves pattern condition association and Or reset behavior; focused expression contract passes 1/1. Module simple-type inference now reverse-searches parameters and returns directly, while flat return values use immutable optionals; focused module-lowering contract passes 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared fld_module_base_sym:316, else_block:628 plus all expressions optionals, and found:257 plus all module optional siblings, then reached imported_mod:770. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/hir-expression-build-23.log, hir-expression-optionals-build-24.log, and module-optionals-build-25.log. Next session: extract relative/canonical import resolution into one value-returning helper or record carrying Module? plus canonical name, preserving direct, relative, and resolve_module_key fallback precedence; add a focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    597, TODO, compiler, P1, "Verify immutable HIR import resolution before resuming the worker.", test/01_unit/compiler/hir/resolve_import_symbols_spec.spl, 17, , "Import lookup now computes direct, relative, then resolve_module_key fallback precedence in resolve_import_module and carries found plus a non-optional Module payload and canonical name, avoiding optional aggregate transport. Relative path construction uses immutable text values and a val segment buffer. The focused source contract passes 1/1. However three functional cycles of resolve_import_symbols_spec fail all six examples, including the five pre-existing direct/glob/alias/qualified cases: answer is unresolved, imported type symbols are nil, and the qualified-call case also references stale HirModule.errors. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/resolve-import-symbols-relative.log through resolve-import-symbols-relative-3.log. The identical broad failure leaves current resolver behavior unverified; no retained-cache worker probe was run after the cap. Next session: isolate one direct provider/consumer fixture against the current HirModule API with resolver diagnostics enabled, determine whether the suite is stale or resolve_import_module loses the module payload, fix once, and require real direct plus relative behavior before any worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588. 2026-08-18: the named spec was re-run to test the \"fails all six examples\" claim but produced NO Results line before the session ended VERDICT: timeout=1 reason=child-timeout budget_ms=900000, Results: 0 total, 0 passed, 0 failed, exit 5. INCONCLUSIVE (nothing executed, so neither confirmed nor refuted) -- but the row's own description is misleading: the spec does NOT reach six failing examples, it HANGS and is killed after the full 900s budget with zero tests executed. Attack the hang, not assertion failures that were never observed. See doc/08_tracking/bug/p1_compiler_first_half_triage_2026-08-18.md", open, true
    598, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after verified import resolution, trait defaults, and MIR dispatch optionals.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/expr_dispatch.spl, 1687, , "Resolver diagnostics proved the immutable module payload is retained; the old broad suite embeds named imports as interpolated strings and references removed HirModule.errors. A current-API focused fixture now concatenates literal braces and proves direct plus relative canonical import registration 2/2. Relative package construction uses segments.slice(...).join rather than mutating a val array; the source contract passes 1/1. Trait default concrete method types now derive through a value-returning helper; source contract passes 1/1 and dispatch behavior passes 3/3. MIR call return, declared return, field-array override, If, and Match optionals are now direct values through one shared lookup helper; focused contract passes 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared imported_mod:770, concrete_symbol_type:213, and ret_out:789 plus all MIR dispatch optional siblings, then reached enum_raw_bool:1687. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/import-resolution-build-26.log, trait-default-type-build-27.log, and mir-dispatch-optionals-build-28.log. Next session: construct enum_raw_bool as a match value, preserving NotEq builder write-back, add a focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    599, TODO, compiler, P1, "Probe the bounded worker after immutable enum and text equality results.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/expr_dispatch.spl, 1687, , "Enum and text Eq/NotEq lowering now constructs the raw result as a match value. Each NotEq arm emits BitXor through a local builder and writes the builder back before returning the inverted local; Eq preserves the original runtime equality local. The expanded MIR dispatch source contract passes 1/1, and entry_closure_defect_semantics_spec passes 13/13 including both enum equality-vs-match cases. The repair was made after the third worker cycle exposed enum_raw_bool, so it is intentionally unprobed under the session cap. Next session: run one retained-cache worker probe using the existing Stage4 runtime and worker cache; run Gate 73 only if that probe emits a fresh replacement worker. No replacement worker exists. Gate 84 remains under macOS TODO 588.", open, true
    600, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after MIR switch/call payload binding repairs.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/switch_operators_calls.spl, 2895, , "Three retained-cache probes cleared enum/text equality, payload_hir_type:1276, and payload_local:1655. The payload paths now use immutable match values, and mir_switch_calls_shared_binding_contract_spec passes 1/1. The final probe reached mutable shared binding str_rendered:2895 before interpreter fallback timed out; logs are enum-text-eq-build-29.log, payload-values-build-30.log, and payload-values-build-31.log. Next session: replace str_rendered with one immutable match/value expression, extend the focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains on the prepared macOS host under TODO 588.", open, true
    601, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after MIR string and method-call shared-binding repairs.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLowering/module_lowering.spl, 1009, , "str_rendered now uses an immutable operand match; result_ok_type and result_err_type use direct conditional values; static_method_id and unresolved_method_id use immutable lookup matches. The focused switch/call and method-call contracts each pass 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared str_rendered:2895, result_ok_type:558, and static_method_id:2208, then reached mutable shared binding init_const:1009. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/str-rendered-build-32.log, result-types-build-33.log, and method-ids-build-34.log. Next session: replace init_const with a direct conditional MirConstant value, add one focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains on the prepared macOS host under TODO 588.", open, true
    602, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after MIR module, LLVM indirect-call, and VHDL entity shared-binding repairs.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vhdl/vhdl_call_lowering.spl, 508, , "init_const and callee_symbol now use immutable matches; indirect-call dest_name and ret_ty use direct conditional values; VHDL entity global symbol discovery uses an immutable match. Their focused contracts each pass 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared init_const:1009, dest_name:380, and symbol:325, then reached mutable shared binding definition:508; the same file has a sibling definition accumulator at line 588. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/init-const-build-35.log, indirect-call-values-build-36.log, and vhdl-symbol-build-37.log. Next session: replace both definition accumulators with value-returning definition lookup while preserving block/index provenance for the first path, add one focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains on the prepared macOS host under TODO 588.", open, true
    603, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after VHDL definition, catalog symbol, and mutation-capability repairs.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/backend_helpers.spl, 253, , "Both VHDL call-definition accumulators now reuse a reverse value-returning lookup that preserves prior last-match behavior; the focused contract passes 1/1. Catalog target resolution tracks a scalar symbol id, and all seven recursive catalog type-marking dictionary parameters declare mut capability; the expanded focused contract passes 1/1. The existing design-catalog behavior suite is blocked in the Rust-seed runner: 19 cases uniformly fail before catalog assertions with semantic dict-to-i64 coercion, one cyclic case reaches an unrelated missing-type assertion, and the independent environment case passes (1/21); log: vhdl-design-catalog-behavior.log. Three retained-cache probes cleared definition:508/588, found:410, and vhdl_catalog_mark_type W1006, then reached mutable shared binding oc:253; adjacent asm_opt:256 has the same write-once optional shape. Probe logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/vhdl-definitions-build-38.log, vhdl-catalog-symbol-build-39.log, and vhdl-catalog-mut-build-40.log. Next session: replace oc and asm_opt with direct conditional values, add one focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains on the prepared macOS host under TODO 588.", open, true
    604, TODO, compiler, P1, "Continue the bounded worker after backend output, interpreter lookup, and VHDL source-selection repairs.", src/compiler/80.driver/driver.spl, 820, , "CompiledModule object-code and assembly optionals now use typed conditional values with implicit lift; the focused contract passes 1/1. Interpreter direct and named call paths now reuse one indexed-or-last-linear value-returning function resolver; its focused contract passes 1/1. VHDL artifact source selection now tracks a scalar index and constructs SourceFile? once; its focused contract passes 1/1. Three retained-cache probes cleared oc:253/asm_opt:256, cf_target_hit:145/cf_named_hit:509, and selected:30, then reached mutable shared binding phase_entry_hir:820. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/backend-output-optionals-build-41.log, interpreter-function-lookup-build-42.log, and vhdl-artifact-source-build-43.log. Next session: track the requested bootstrap entry source index as an integer during the phase-3 loop, derive phase_entry_hir once from phase_hir_modules after lowering, and preserve self.ctx.bootstrap_entry_hir when no requested entry appears; add one focused contract, then run one retained-cache worker probe. No replacement worker exists; do not run Gate 73. Gate 84 remains on the prepared macOS host under TODO 588.", open, true
    605, TODO, compiler, P1, "Register the monotonic-time runtime provider for the source-matched Cranelift JIT worker.", src/runtime/runtime_time.c, 1, , "rt_time_now_monotonic_ms now belongs to the modular C runtime and is registered by simple-runtime; duplicate native_all ownership was removed. rt_panic now has a Rust provider and canonical registry entry. Both focused generated-table tests pass, the incrementally rebuilt release seed exports both symbols, and probe 47 cleared both unresolved JIT externals. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/runtime-monotonic-provider-test.log, release-seed-panic-provider-build.log, and panic-provider-build-47.log.", done, false
    606, TODO, compiler, P1, "Keep native-build entry-closure discovery from admitting unrelated sanitized-path duplicates.", src/compiler/80.driver/driver.spl, 503, , "Bounded provenance proved the 452-file requested closure had no llm_caret edge; the unrelated ant-trace collision came from whole-workspace fallback. SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_ENTRY was present while the duplicated CompileOptions.mode arrived as nil, so the redundant Aot comparison skipped closure handling. Native-entry presence now owns that gate, and explicit walks mark closure mode even when they report an error. The isolated regression passes 1/1. Probe 49 cleared the collision and reached the real VHDL parser blocker. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/worker-closure-provenance.log, worker-closure-mode-trace.log, and mode-owner-build-49.log.", done, false
    607, TODO, compiler, P1, "Resolve qualified HirLowering method calls in the Rust-seed Cranelift worker.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/codegen/instr/closures_structs.rs, 421, , "Qualified MethodCallStatic recursion now bypasses the self-recursion guard that remains required for ambiguous bare calls. The object-level regression proves HirLowering.lower_hir_expr resolves without an rt_function_not_found relocation, and the focused Rust test passes 1/1. Incremental release-seed build passes. Corrected retained-cache probe 57 emits zero lower_hir_expr or scan_ast_expr_for_returns not-found errors and advances beyond the old failure. Logs: build/gpu-goal/source-matched/rust-trace-build-55.log and qualified-recursion-build-57.log.", done, false
    608, TODO, compiler, P1, "Finish the source-matched native worker after closure parser repairs.", src/app/cli/bootstrap_focused_native_build.spl, 9, , "Retained-cache probe 182 used no bootstrap, cache reset, or retry, but is not comparable to probe 179: it emitted phase1:load_sources:start and made no further phase-profile progress before the 600 s timeout, whereas probe 179 completed phase 1 in 64.589 s. Post-run host evidence showed load averages 26.40/30.19/28.82 on 32 CPUs, full configured swap, and several concurrent 98-180 percent CPU native-build, test, lint, and GHDL jobs; do not infer a source or HIR regression from this contaminated run. Phase-1 profiling now reports each input root start/done, the seeded source total, closure start/done, and closure progress every 64 sources. The loading owner and full driver registration path check, and the expanded source ownership contract passes 7/7. No fresh worker exists. A 2026-07-31 preflight correctly blocked another probe: 7 GiB of 8 GiB swap was used, an initial broad scan saw six native-build-related command lines, and the hardened exact scanner found two active native-build executables. The shared heavy-work preflight now inspects exact argv[1] values, rejects overlapping native-build executables, and fails closed when process inspection is unavailable. Its SPipe contract includes fake-proc behavioral cases for exact counting and detector failure. Next session: wait for an isolated host, then run exactly one retained-cache phase-profiled probe with timeout 600, no bootstrap, retry, or cache reset. Use the new markers to identify the exact input root or closure interval if phase 1 stalls; if parsing resumes, record the next measured parser wall. If fresh, compile native_build_worker.spl and only then run Gate 73. Do not reset build/gpu-goal/source-matched/worker-cache. Rust-seed transient heap promotion is now registered in interpreter dispatch, JIT/runtime symbol manifests, ELF lookup, and SFFI ABI metadata. The missing mem-guard heap-owner accessor is repaired and compiler unit compilation advances through simple-runtime into simple-compiler. A focused direct `[u32]` parameter-index MIR regression now requires typed raw-word access, unsigned narrowing, and no boxed array/index dispatch. Under host load 62 on 32 CPUs, the bounded 120-second runtime and 180-second compiler runs timed out before test execution; do not claim behavior PASS. Re-run the focused tests and streaming lifecycle examples when the host is isolated. Gate 84 remains under TODO 588. Logs: focused-worker-build-179.log, focused-worker-build-182.log, source-load-phase-profile-contract-183.log, hir-pipeline-split-contract-180.log, and hir-streaming-owner-contract-181-fixed.log.", open, true
    609, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate pure-Simple Vulkan control, memory barrier, and integer value lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 170, , "Workgroup and subgroup MIR barriers emit OpControlBarrier with SPIR-V scope constants 2/3 and Vulkan memory-semantics masks 264/2376. Workgroup and Device MIR fences emit OpMemoryBarrier with scopes 2/1 and the same legal masks; fence-only modules are recognized as compute shaders. Device-wide control barriers fail closed because one dispatch cannot synchronize all workgroups. QueueFamily fences fail closed because the module uses legacy GLSL450 rather than the Vulkan memory model, and All/CrossDevice fails because Vulkan shader memory scope excludes CrossDevice. U32 and source-level I64 constants, copies, moves, Add/Sub/Mul, inline integer operands, and real I64 invocation-ID data flow now lower through a live local-to-SPIR-V value map. GpuBlockDim lowers the fixed LocalSize values as typed constants, while GpuGridDim conditionally exposes Vulkan NumWorkgroups and participates in the same U32/I64 value flow. I64 shaders request Int64 and zero-extend Vulkan U32 invocation IDs into an unsigned 64-bit carrier; the supported arithmetic is sign-agnostic. Constants are predeclared for SPIR-V logical layout but become live only at their MIR instruction, so use-before-definition fails closed. The focused intensive spec pins exact constant/value IDs, covers inline operands, use-before-definition, range, destination-type and dimension rejection, compile_module retention, and runs spirv-as plus spirv-val when available. On this host, exact standalone synchronization and I64 invocation/arithmetic modules pass spirv-as/spirv-val for Vulkan 1.3. The stale Rust bootstrap seed passed 19/26 cases before the final destination-type case was added, but reproduced its known constant-cache defect in all seven constant-dependent cases, so it is not accepted as behavior evidence. One retained-cache pure-Simple CLI build compiled the Vulkan module but failed on 16 unrelated app/library files. Keep open until a deployed source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes test/01_unit/compiler/backend/vulkan_backend_intensive_spec.spl.", done, false
    610, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate pure-Simple CUDA GPU index typing and register allocation.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda_backend.spl, 443, , "Normal MIR lowers global/local/block/block-dimension/grid-dimension IDs as I64, while the CUDA backend previously wrote mov.u32/add.u32 results directly into .s64 locals and generated temporary registers from r0, colliding with fixed MIR-local registers. The backend now reserves every local register ID before allocating temporaries, accepts only U32/I64/U64 index destinations, rejects dimensions outside 0..2 with typed CUDA errors, and recognizes block/grid-dimension-only kernels. I64/U64 global IDs zero-extend thread, block, and block-size components before 64-bit multiply/add, avoiding U32 overflow; non-global I64/U64 IDs use typed conversion and U32 stays direct. The intensive contract covers all five I64 operations, U64 global arithmetic, direct U32, fallback kernel detection, invalid dimension/type rejection, exact register non-collision, and ptxas when installed. On this host, the exact standalone mixed I64/U64/U32 module passes ptxas -arch=sm_86. No accepted pure-Simple focused test run exists because the deployed full CLI remains unavailable under TODO 608; keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes test/01_unit/compiler/codegen/cuda_backend_intensive_contract_spec.spl.", done, false
    611, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate pure-Simple CUDA indexed-kernel bounds checks.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda_backend.spl, 422, , "Ordinary MIR indexed access emits bounds_check(index, length), but CUDA previously rejected the intrinsic before otherwise-supported load/store lowering. CUDA now accepts exactly two operands with no destination, widens signed or unsigned integer indices to the runtime-compatible I64 comparison domain, requires an I64 length, and emits predicated traps for index < 0 and index >= length. Non-integer indices, non-I64 lengths, malformed arity, and destination-bearing forms fail closed with typed CUDA errors. The focused stale-seed run passed all three new bounds-check cases, including I64/I32/U32/U64 conversion coverage and source-generated PTX assembly with ptxas, while three unrelated pre-existing seed-semantic cases failed (13/16 overall); the independent exact I32-widening PTX also passes ptxas -arch=sm_86. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the full intensive spec.", done, false
    612, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate pure-Simple Vulkan indexed Workgroup memory lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 153, , "Fixed U32 GpuSharedAlloc now emits deterministic Workgroup array/type/variable declarations, lists used Workgroup variables in the SPIR-V 1.4+ OpEntryPoint interface, lowers one-index U32/I64 GEPs to OpAccessChain, and permits typed U32 stores/loads through only those lowered mutable element pointers. GEP indices must be statically in range or derive from a local-invocation ID/copy whose workgroup bound fits the allocation; arbitrary and out-of-range indices fail closed. Invalid element/destination types, mutability, sizes, duplicate destinations, GEP arity/base/index types, and load/store value shapes also fail closed. SPIR-V Tools are mandatory for the focused validator cases. Race-free exact standalone single- and multi-allocation/index/store/load modules pass spirv-as and spirv-val for Vulkan 1.3. The final stale-seed focused run passed 21/31 cases; both valid shared-memory cases reached spirv-val but reproduced the documented seed closure-cache defect by dropping type/constant declarations, while the allocation/pointer fail-closed cases present in that run passed. The later bounds-proof cases remain source-reviewed under the three-cycle cap. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the intensive spec, then extend the established pointer map to Vulkan atomics and additional element types.", done, false
    613, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate pure-Simple Vulkan U32 Workgroup atomic lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 548, , "The Vulkan backend now lowers Add, Sub, And, Or, Xor, unsigned Min/Max, Exchange, and CompareExchange through validated U32 Workgroup pointers with Workgroup scope and AcquireRelease WorkgroupMemory semantics; compare-exchange uses Acquire WorkgroupMemory failure semantics. Atomic results remain live MIR values, generic compare-exchange and malformed pointer/type shapes fail closed, and the focused race-free spec pins every opcode and validates emitted SPIR-V when tools are available. The stale-seed run passed 21/33 overall: malformed atomic cases passed and exact opcode assertions reached the validator, but the positive case reproduced TODO 612's known dropped declaration defect. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the intensive spec.", done, false
    614, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate source-matched CUDA pointer address-space lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda_backend.spl, 224, , "CUDA shared allocations previously materialized generic shared addresses but Load, Store, GpuAtomicOp, GpuAtomicCas, typed atomic intrinsics, and vector memory intrinsics always emitted global-memory PTX. The backend now tracks global kernel arguments, shared allocations, and local allocations per function; propagates provenance through copy, move, cast, bitcast, and GEP; converts generic shared addresses back with cvta.to.shared before shared operations; rejects pointers without provenance and local-memory atomics; validates allocation, scalar memory, generic atomic, typed atomic, and F32 vector-store pointer/value/index types; restricts generic atomics to 32/64-bit integers; emits CAS/exchange/bitwise suffixes at PTX bit width; maps signed-I64 add/sub to PTX's legal U64 modulo form; leaves device-function pointer parameters unproven; and rejects multi-block shared/local origins until CFG dataflow exists. Kernel/device entry classification now uses explicit MIR/adaptor intent instead of reclassifying device functions from their instructions. Vector loads fail closed until MIR can represent their result instead of discarding loaded values and writing zero; vector stores require exact arity and no destination. An exact shared module covering U32 load/store/add/sub/CAS/bitwise, I32 add/min/max/exchange, and U64/I64 add/min/max passes CUDA 13 ptxas for sm_86. The repaired focused source contract now passes 4/4 on the current cached Rust-seed runner, including pointer-space and vector source ownership. The stale-seed intensive runs reached fail-closed cases but retained an older four-argument backend method for the positive path, while three unrelated pre-existing cases also failed. A direct file check timed out under the 60-second CPU guard, and focused lint hit its internal zero-second timeout. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the focused pointer and vector behavior specs and generated PTX passes ptxas.", done, false
    615, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate source-matched Vulkan compute entry ABI rejection.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 132, , "Vulkan compute entry points now reject fixed or variadic parameters until StorageBuffer interface lowering exists, require a Unit signature, reject hidden argument/return locals, and reject Ret(Some(...)) even when malformed MIR claims a Unit return. Annotated Vulkan kernels are selected before validation even without GPU instructions, while explicitly targeted non-Vulkan kernels remain excluded. The direct adapter rejects every nonzero argument count before indexing locals. The shared compile_compute_shader owner covers compile_module and direct compile_kernel paths. The final updated source contract passes 2/2. The cached intensive suite parses and runs all 36 cases but remains 24/36 because its Rust-seed backend is stale; no bootstrap or retry was used, and the three-cycle cap is exhausted. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the focused intensive ABI cases without bootstrap.", done, false
    616, TODO, runtime, P1, "Deploy Vulkan native non-main compute entry propagation on all supported hosts.", src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/vulkan_graphics_runtime_shader.rs, 173, , "The native Vulkan provider previously discarded the requested entry name while ComputePipeline hardcoded main, diverging from the interpreter and compiler-emitted function names. The provider now decodes exact tagged or raw Simple text, including raw pointers whose low bits resemble heap tags; validates empty/NUL names before Vulkan allocation; passes the requested name into VkPipelineShaderStageCreateInfo; rejects signed push sizes outside u32 before casting and validates alignment plus the selected device limit; cleans every partially constructed Vulkan object on failure; and keeps the legacy rt_vk_kernel_compile API explicitly on main. Both dynamic Engine2D providers now reject invalid entry text, retain an explicitly NUL-terminated entry buffer, and pass all three ABI arguments. Focused Rust decoding and entry validation pass 1/1 each, the Vulkan-feature runtime check passes, and the pre-final source contract passes 3/3. The explicitly hardware-required live test passes 1/1 on the current NVIDIA Vulkan host: its valid non-main-only SPIR-V module rejects main and successfully creates custom_compute_entry. The final range guard was source-reviewed after the three-cycle verification cap and was not rerun. Keep open until a source-matched runtime archive passes final focused checks, deployment, and the same live test on every supported Vulkan host.", open, true
    617, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate source-matched CUDA MIR comparison operand typing.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda_backend.spl, 329, , "Normal MIR comparison destinations are Bool, but CUDA previously passed that result type into compile_binop and emitted invalid setp predicates such as setp.lt.pred. The shared instruction owner now derives PTX comparison suffixes from matching operands, requires a Bool destination, and accepts only PTX-supported I32/I64/U32/U64/F32/F64 comparison types. The source contract passes 1/1. Focused U32/I64/U64/F32 exact PTX and ptxas pass, as do malformed non-Bool destination, mismatched operand, and predicate operand cases. The cached Rust-seed suite passes 16/22 overall; its six failures are pre-existing register-allocation, call-lowering, and stale pointer-signature cases outside this slice. Keep open until the same focused behavior passes under a source-matched pure-Simple compiler.", done, false
    618, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate self-contained generated portable Metal MSL modules.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/gpu_portable_compute.spl, 487, , "Portable Metal kernels previously began with bare kernel declarations, and the combined generated 2D module concatenated them without #include <metal_stdlib> or using namespace metal. The shared source wrapper now prepends the Metal standard-library prelude to standalone generic emitters while leaving CUDA, HIP, OpenCL, and WebGPU unchanged; combined Metal output removes per-kernel copies and restores exactly one module prelude. The isolated behavioral spec passes 1/1 and pins standalone fill/add/scroll preludes, exactly one combined prelude, all five entry signatures and buffer bindings, plus non-Metal exclusion. The independent source contract passes 1/1. The older broad portable-compute suite timed out before assertions under the stale Rust-seed runner and was not retried. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the focused specs and the prepared metallib/readback gate passes on macOS under TODO 588.", done, false
    619, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate source-matched CUDA bitcast width lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda_backend.spl, 472, , "CUDA Bitcast previously hardcoded mov.b64 for every source and target, so valid F32-to-U32 and U32-to-F32 MIR produced width-invalid PTX. The shared instruction owner now requires exact destination/target MIR-kind equality, accepts only 32-bit or 64-bit scalar/pointer sources and targets, rejects width mismatches and predicates, emits mov.b32 or mov.b64 from the validated width, and preserves existing pointer-space propagation. The final focused source contract passes 1/1 on the current cached Rust-seed runner after exact-kind strengthening. Both intensive behavior cases pass, including exact F32/U32 and F64/U64 PTX, ptxas assembly, target/width mismatch rejection, and predicate rejection. The cached Rust-seed suite passes 18/24 overall; its six failures are the same pre-existing register-allocation, call-lowering, and stale pointer-signature cases outside this slice. A final higher-model review found Unit could collapse to I64; width selection now matches exact MIR kinds and the Unit rejection case is present. Keep open until a source-matched pure-Simple compiler passes the final focused behavior.", done, false
    620, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate source-matched CUDA unsigned negation lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda/ptx_builder.spl, 285, , "Valid U32/U64 MIR negation previously emitted neg.u32/neg.u64 even though PTX neg accepts signed integer types only. The shared PTX emitter now preserves modulo-width semantics with sub.u32/sub.u64 destination, zero, source while retaining signed and floating neg lowering. The focused source contract passes 1/1. The exact U32/U64 behavior case and ptxas assembly pass; after the unary expansion the cached Rust-seed intensive suite passes 21/27 overall with the same six pre-existing register-allocation, call-lowering, and stale pointer-signature failures. Keep open until the focused behavior passes under a source-matched pure-Simple compiler.", done, false
    621, TODO, compiler, P1, "Validate source-matched CUDA unary type and BitNot lowering.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/cuda_backend.spl, 346, , "HIR valid bitwise complement previously failed closed because CUDA rejected MirUnaryOp.BitNot, while I8/U8 and malformed unary shapes could reach invalid PTX. CUDA now requires exact destination/operand MIR-kind equality; restricts logical Not to Bool; accepts Neg only for legal I16/I32/I64/U16/U32/U64/F32/F64 forms; lowers unsigned U16/U32/U64 negation as modulo-width subtraction; emits PTX not.b16/b32/b64 for signed or unsigned 16/32/64-bit BitNot; and rejects 8-bit, pointer, float-BitNot, integer-Not, and mismatched forms before emission. The Bool parameter loader now zero-extends ld.param.u8 into U16 and uses legal setp.ne.u16 instead of unsupported setp.ne.u8. The expanded source contract passes 1/1. Both focused positive/fail-closed cases pass, including ptxas for U16 negation, Bool Not, and every supported BitNot width/sign; the cached Rust-seed intensive suite passes 21/27 overall with the same six pre-existing failures. Keep open until the final focused behavior passes under a source-matched pure-Simple compiler.", done, false
    622, TODO, gpu, P1, "Remove canonical SDN serialization from repeated primary web Draw IR route-key lookups without weakening exact identity.", doc/08_tracking/perf/web_draw_ir_route_key_sdn_overhead_2026-07-30.md, 1, , "The retained 64/256/1024-command benchmark passes with three warmups, three measured samples, stable encoded-size assertions, and final medians of 317359/1269513/4937136 us for 30571/121514/485835 SDN bytes under the source-matched incremental Rust interpreter. Earlier independent runs measured 345428/1312451/5307734 us and 305251/1207284/4820833 us. Two portable full-structure hash attempts timed out on two-command fixtures and a runtime text_hash variant was unavailable; all production changes were restored after the three-cycle cap. Next session: add an opaque revision to SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult, owned by SimpleWebRenderSession, covering document/style revisions, viewport dimensions, resolved font and registry generation, render configuration, asset root, render-budget state, and ordered composition semantics. Use a session-owned cache or key the process-local cache by exact session identity plus composition revision; never reuse degraded or partial output. Standalone, animated, scrolled, overlay, and image-backed paths retain exact SDN keys or disable reuse until owner-scoped revisions exist. Require paired same-host/runtime lower medians plus unchanged CUDA parity. Keep Metal evidence under TODO 588.", open, true
    623, TODO, gpu, P1, "Complete native hosted browser process/pipe measurement with an admitted executable.", test/05_perf/browser/hosted_browser_process_pipe_perf_spec.spl, 1, , "Absolute source and worker paths pin native runs to the GPU worktree. Generated wrappers use _native.spl, consecutive top-level declarations stay before generated main, and receiver/result types are explicit. High-model review found and fixed the fallback duplicate-evaluation risk, and the weak regression was replaced with non-flattened package imports. The focused compiler test remains unexecuted and timed out during simple-compiler compilation; do not claim this fix passed. Retained log: /tmp/hosted-process-pipe-native-owned-20260730-final.log. Resume with one source-matched focused compiler check, then run one native-mode measurement using absolute SIMPLE_LIB and SIMPLE_HOSTED_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE paths from an admitted source-matched executable. Require canonical preinit sandboxing, exact producer generation and composition revision, changed/stable pixels, exact render/reuse counters, and unchanged p50 below changed p50. Do not substitute interpreter timing or claim timing from zero samples.", open, true
    624, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run the positive Vulkan SFFI compute launch and device readback regression within a bounded build.", src/compiler_rust/runtime/tests/vulkan_sffi_tests.rs, 342, , "PASS: the embedded SPIR-V 1.3 single-invocation storage-buffer kernel passes spirv-val. With incremental codegen disabled to isolate stale shared objects, the final lifecycle implementation passed the bounded physical-device gate 1/1 on NVIDIA RTX A6000 (DISCRETE_GPU): upload 0xdeadbeef, compile, launch, synchronize, exact GPU-written 0x12345678 download, and all cleanup succeeded. The regression prints name/type, cleans all handles before asserting the physical-device requirement, and uses SIMPLE_REQUIRE_PHYSICAL_VULKAN=1 to reject software ICDs. Retained log: /tmp/vulkan-positive-physical-device-isolated.log.", done, false
    625, TODO, gpu, P1, "Require CUDA draw_text to prove device execution instead of accepting CPU fallback pixels.", test/integration/rendering/cuda_strict_spec.spl, 368, , "PASS: draw_text now reads Engine2D provenance and requires source=device_readback, positive backend_handle, positive device_identity, exact framebuffer length, and non-background glyph pixels. The filtered interpreter command still executed the full strict file and passed 25/25 on the live CUDA host. Native SMF compilation remains unavailable for this broad fixture because 150 existing functions require interpreter constructs. Retained log: /tmp/cuda-strict-device-readback-3.log.", done, false
    626, TODO, gpu, P1, "Harden the remaining Vulkan graphics, presentation, and completion-unknown ownership paths.", src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/gpu_vulkan/vulkan_sffi/command.rs, 59, , "Legacy compute and graphics commands now retain exact Arc owners, originating devices, fences, command buffers, descriptor resources, buffers, pipelines, and exact framebuffer attachments through completion-unknown quarantine. Device switching rejects live device resources; idle/shutdown cleanup fails closed; stale draw/submit/discard handles are rejected. Direct ComputePipeline execution accepts owned buffer Arcs, retains pipeline/fence/command/buffers, blocks buffer/image I/O while uncertain, and retries descriptor recovery after successful device idle. wait_hardware_idle locks each distinct compute, graphics, and present queue before vkDeviceWaitIdle; SFFI submit uses its graphics queue mutex. SFFI recovery preserves uncertain commands, rejects device free while commands are live, and clears uncertainty only after proven hardware idle; incremental simple-runtime Vulkan check including tests PASS. Offline simple-native-all with Vulkan also PASS, proving the prior rspirv build-script blocker false. The source contract used a Rust-seed runner, so no pure-Simple runner claim is made. Transfer and direct-compute recovery now use a cycle-free DeviceLifetime, raw transfer-owner quarantine, shared recovery admission gate, partial-build cleanup guard, and fail-closed lifetime leaks. Focused Vulkan runtime tests pass 9/9 and independent high-model ownership/lock review passed; deterministic recovery-state tests cover preservation and exactly-once reaping, but no claim is made for real-device failed-drop injection. Separate-family presentation and prepared macOS execution remain open.", open, true
    627, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run admitted CUDA, Vulkan, and Metal CPU/GPU break-even measurements.", test/03_system/app/simpleos_gpu_host/processing_ir_offload_break_even_spec.spl, 1, , "PARTIAL: canonical CUDA FillU32 live evidence passes on NVIDIA RTX A6000 with exact readback and no crossing through 1048576 elements, so automatic CUDA offload remains disabled. Vulkan FillU32 live evidence on NVIDIA TITAN RTX crosses at 65536 elements with exact readback. Compiler-produced Vulkan SPIR-V also dispatches with exact physical-device readback, while source-matched cleanup qualification remains under TODO 647. Keep open only for the prepared-macOS Metal FillU32 measurement; never substitute CPU mirrors or unavailable receipts.", open, true
    630, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run the Metal CPU/GPU break-even measurement on a prepared macOS host.", test/03_system/app/simpleos_gpu_host/processing_ir_offload_break_even_spec.spl, 1, , "This row is macOS-hardware-only: Linux source contracts, CPU mirrors, unavailable receipts, and Metal library compilation do not measure device execution. Close only with paired CPU/GPU samples, real Metal device identity, exact device readback, communication-overhead accounting, and a retained receipt from the canonical macOS host gate.", open, true
    631, TODO, compiler, P1, "Repair Vulkan source ABI argument-local type divergence.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLowering/function_lowering.spl, 177, , "DONE: once primitive Vulkan metadata reaches MIR, the source spec passes signature and argument-local Ptr/U32 assertions and advances into backend entry validation. The earlier Array tag was caused by metadata transport, not MirBuilder local divergence.", done, false
    632, TODO, compiler, P1, "Prevent Vulkan GEP mutability escalation from immutable StorageBuffers.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 625, , "DONE: Vulkan GEP lowering rejects mutable destinations derived from immutable StorageBuffer arguments before Store. The focused negative MIR regression passes in the containing intensive suite.", done, false
    633, TODO, compiler, P1, "Require a Vulkan signature-to-argument-local bijection.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 176, , "DONE: entry validation rejects missing, duplicate, negative, out-of-range, and type-mismatched argument locals before interface generation. Focused malformed MIR cases pass in the containing intensive suite.", done, false
    634, TODO, compiler, P1, "Preserve GPU metadata for direct MIR lowering callers.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/jit_interpreter.spl, 173, , "DONE: the public lower_function wrapper forwards is_gpu_kernel, gpu_target, and gpu_backend_order to the primitive metadata entrypoint. JIT uses that wrapper; positional, named-target, backend-order, and complete-module regressions pass.", done, false
    635, TODO, compiler, P2, "Correct the Vulkan invalid-element diagnostic assertion.", test/01_unit/compiler/backend/vulkan_source_storage_buffer_abi_spec.spl, 80, , "DONE: the expectation matches the implementation's exact 'require U32 elements' wording. The focused invalid-i32 source case passes under the cache-free verifier.", done, false
    636, TODO, compiler, P1, "Repair HIR GPU metadata transport into MirLowering.", doc/08_tracking/bug/pure_simple_hir_module_gpu_metadata_transport_loss_2026-07-31.md, 1, , "DONE: the actual loss was a stale Rust-seed impl-method cache index. After validating and rebuilding stale indices, source Vulkan ABI passes 3/3, complete-module metadata passes 9/9, and emitted assembly passes spirv-as plus spirv-val. All temporary MirLowering transport arrays were removed and the normal path retained the same PASS.", done, false
    637, TODO, compiler, P1, "Preserve source Unit returns for Vulkan entry lowering.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLowering/function_lowering.spl, 361, , "DONE: HIR and MIR signature assertions both prove Unit. Shared function lowering now emits Ret(nil) for Unit signatures even when trailing () lowered to a temporary. The Vulkan cannot-return-a-value failure is gone; the source endpoint advances to an unrelated Infer body-type diagnostic.", done, false
    638, TODO, compiler, P1, "Repair Vulkan source parameter diagnostics after metadata transport.", src/compiler/50.mir/mir_lowering_stmts.spl, 1144, , "DONE: the immutable-buffer guard reports target.span, and the invalid-i32 plus immutable-write source cases both pass under the cache-free verifier. The remaining positive-case harness failure is unrelated to diagnostics.", done, false
    639, TODO, compiler, P1, "Resolve inferred body types in source Vulkan kernels.", src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLowering/function_lowering.spl, 524, , "DONE: unannotated let bindings treat HirTypeKind.Infer as absent and recover the initializer MIR type; the Vulkan gpu_global_id local becomes U32. The Infer diagnostic is gone and the positive source kernel emits retained SPIR-V assembly.", done, false
    640, TODO, compiler, P1, "Invalidate stale Rust-seed impl method indices.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/interpreter_method/special/execution.rs, 46, , "DONE: cached impl-method indices are accepted only when the current registry still contains the requested method at that index; stale entries rebuild from the current slice. The reordered-registry unit regression passes 1/1, source Vulkan ABI passes 3/3, and complete-module metadata passes 9/9 through the rebuilt seed.", done, false
    641, TODO, gpu, P1, "Use measured backend break-even thresholds in SimpleOS GPU offload policy.", src/app/simpleos_gpu_host/daemon_runner.spl, 31, , "PARTIAL: absent CLI overrides select the measured Vulkan FillU32 threshold of 65536 elements. Canonical CUDA FillU32 measurement found no crossing through 1048576 elements, so its default remains 536870912, one above the maximum valid request, and automatic CUDA offload stays disabled by evidence. Metal uses the same fail-closed default until prepared-macOS calibration. Explicit zero and non-negative overrides remain authoritative.", open, true
    642, TODO, gpu, P1, "Fail closed when Vulkan swapchain idle recovery fails.", src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/vulkan/swapchain.rs, 369, , "DONE: Drop logs and returns before destroying image views or swapchain when wait_idle fails. The simplified completion-recovery contract passes 4/4.", done, false
    643, TODO, gpu, P2, "Preserve Metal aliases and VHDL exclusion in GPU target selection.", test/01_unit/compiler/semantics/gpu_target_contract_spec.spl, 37, , "DONE: metal, msl, and metal-shading-language produce identical valid Metal selections; vhdl and fpga remain normalized but unsupported GPU kernel targets with empty backend order. The full target contract passes 6/6.", done, false
    644, TODO, compiler, P1, "Produce and execute CUDA PTX from a source global-pointer kernel.", test/02_integration/rendering/cuda_compiler_ptx_live_spec.spl, 1, , "DONE: frontend-to-MIR CUDA array parameters lower to global pointers, skip host runtime-array metadata and bounds calls, and raw-pointer indexing emits GEP/load/store. The source suite passes 3/3 for write/read/immutability and host-call exclusion. The strict hardware integration passes 1/1 through the incrementally rebuilt diagnostic seed: compiler-produced PTX loads, launches fill on CUDA, synchronizes, and reads back eight exact device-written 42 values. The stale accepted bin/simple cannot yet compile this new source ABI and was not bootstrapped in this lane.", done, false
    645, TODO, gpu, P1, "Measure CUDA FillU32 CPU/GPU break-even for the production ProcessingIr operation.", test/05_perf/local_gpu_check/cuda_fill_u32_break_even.c, 1, , "DONE: the canonical output-only checker passed live on NVIDIA RTX A6000 with real device UUID/identity, exact readback, zero mismatches, 3 warmups, 5 measured samples, RSS, and hashes binding source, executable, PTX, raw samples, device identity, and coverage. CPU remained faster at 4096 (2 us vs 212 us), 65536 (19 us vs 311 us), and 1048576 (2405 us vs 6319 us), so no crossing was observed through the required coverage bound. Automatic CUDA offload correctly remains disabled; forcing it would regress this production FillU32 workload.", done, false
    646, TODO, compiler, P1, "Bind Vulkan storage descriptors by argument index rather than local-array order.", src/compiler/70.backend/backend/vulkan_backend.spl, 247, , "DONE: each storage local derives its binding from the pointer ordinal in the validated signature, so reordered Arg locals cannot reverse descriptors. The new behavioral regression passed within the intensive suite; that broad run was 39/42 because three unrelated pre-existing assertions failed.", done, false
    647, TODO, compiler, P1, "Expose compiler-produced Vulkan SPIR-V to cross-package live qualification.", test/02_integration/rendering/vulkan_compiler_spirv_live_qualification_spec.spl, 1, , "PARTIAL: vulkan_compile_module_direct is the minimal public Vulkan 1.3/default-options producer. A fresh strict run on the physical NVIDIA RTX A6000 again compiled source through HIR/MIR, assembled and validated the exact output, dispatched it, and read back eight exact 42 values. Buffer release and shutdown reaping passed. Pipeline and shader cleanup still reported false because the deployed bin/simple predates the source-fixed interpreter bool ABI; its 2026-07-25 binary cannot prove the current 2026-07-31 wrapper source. Keep open under TODO 580 until a source-matched incremental self-hosted deploy is admitted, then rerun this gate once.", open, true
    648, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run the production Simple ProcessingIR Vulkan FillU32 executor on Linux hardware.", test/02_integration/rendering/processing_ir_vulkan_fill_u32_live_spec.spl, 1, , "IMPLEMENTED, EXECUTION BLOCKED: the strict spec calls processing_ir_execute_vulkan directly and requires 64 exact device-written 0xA1B2C3D4 values, positive backend/device identity, and no CPU/C fallback. The current deployed bin/simple rejects the current Vulkan dependency-quarantine extern before executing the example, so no live result is claimed. Keep open under TODO 580 until a source-matched self-hosted deploy is admitted, then run this spec once.", open, true
    649, TODO, gpu, P1, "Prove Vulkan ProcessingIR completion-unknown quarantine recovery.", src/lib/gc_async_mut/processing/vulkan_fill_u32.spl, 108, , "PARTIAL: a gated dispatch-ineligible phase now drives status zero and the normal owned cleanup path without calling the dispatch SFFI; exact phase mapping and the expanded native contract pass. A proposed pre-dispatch completion-unknown injection was rejected because it would falsely transfer resources to quarantine without an accepted or uncertain GPU submission. Keep open until a source-matched physical-Vulkan fault can induce an actual post-submit unknown-completion result, then prove quarantine preservation, device-idle reaping, exact recovery readback, stable identity, and successful shutdown.", open, true
    650, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run source-matched CUDA same-executor submit, readback, and mismatch recovery.", src/app/test/processing_cuda_fill_probe.spl, 32, , "IMPLEMENTED, EXECUTION BLOCKED by TODO 651. The probe/wrapper require exact baseline output, typed injected failure with empty output and zero provenance, then exact same-executor recovery with stable positive handle/device identity. On 2026-08-02 the third and final GPU-renderer build cycle cleared the explicit /test/ entry-filter failure but hit the bounded 600-second timeout without producing a source-matched candidate. Canonical CUDA fill/parity wrappers were therefore not rerun and no new device PASS is claimed. Retained log: build/simpleos_gpu_host/cuda_fill_native/gpu-renderer-cycle3.log. Resume with the exact native-build command in the CUDA operator manual using a source-matched compiled worker, then run the canonical wrapper once. Merge owner/final reviewer: root Codex agent at normal/highest capability.", open, true
    651, TODO, compiler, P1, "Keep explicit-entry native builds on the true transitive closure before MIR validation.", src/app/cli/bootstrap_main.spl, 112, , "PARTIAL, RUNTIME PROOF BLOCKED: the 2026-08-02 CUDA lane found that _driver_collect_sources unconditionally discarded an explicit entry under /test/. It now exempts only the exact SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_ENTRY while retaining broad test-directory filtering; the focused source regression passes 1/1. Cycle-3 log analysis shows no closure/driver phase marker at all: 1,500+ lines are warnings while the stale Rust seed interprets src/app/cli/native_build_worker.spl and loads its whole compiler plus LLVM graph before cli_native_build begins. Evidence includes cross-module collisions for compiler inference/codegen/linking plus gc warnings for llvm_loader, dynamic, daemon_sdk, CUDA, and Vulkan. This matches native_build_main.spl's explicit contract that interpreted workers load the whole compiler graph before codegen; the 600-second outer timeout expired in worker bootstrap, not in the requested ProcessingIR closure. No focused owner-boundary code fix is justified: narrowing compile_targets closure cannot affect work performed before that function executes. Do not run a fourth cycle in the same session. Retained log: build/simpleos_gpu_host/cuda_fill_native/gpu-renderer-cycle3.log. Narrow resume probe on a fresh admitted pure-Simple compiled CLI: SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_TRACE_CLOSURE=1 SIMPLE_NATIVE_BUILD_TRACE_CLOSURE_TIMING=1 SIMPLE_COMPILER_TRACE=1 bin/simple native-build --source src/compiler --source src/app --source src/lib --entry-closure --entry src/app/test/processing_cuda_fill_probe.spl --cache-dir build/simpleos_gpu_host/cuda_fill_native/cache --strip --output build/simpleos_gpu_host/cuda_fill_native/processing_cuda_fill_probe. Require the first closure-entry marker, bounded visited/queued counts, and a produced candidate; if the command still enters interpreted-worker bootstrap, stop and redeploy the compiled CLI rather than increasing the timeout. Merge owner: compiler native-build lane. Final reviewer: highest-capability model.", open, true
    652, TODO, gpu, P1, "Admit generated ProcessingIR and Metal-to-Metal drawing MSL with native device readback on macOS.", test/03_system/app/simple_2d/feature/processing_metal_msl_backend_spec.spl, 1, , "OPEN, EXECUTION BLOCKED: Linux proves deterministic source and fail-closed metadata only; both native rows deliberately fail. Target hardware: physical Apple Silicon or Intel Mac with a Metal compute GPU. Required libraries/provider: Metal.framework, Foundation.framework, CoreGraphics.framework, objc2-metal runtime, and Simple Metal SFFI. Toolchain: Xcode Command Line Tools with xcrun metal/metallib plus admitted source-matched pure-Simple bin/simple. Probe exactly: xcrun --find metal; xcrun --find metallib. Resume exactly: SIMPLE_LIB=src bin/simple test test/03_system/app/simple_2d/feature/processing_metal_msl_backend_spec.spl --mode=interpreter. Retain compiled artifacts/raw readback/oracle/mismatch/latency/RSS under build/gpu_renderer_processing_backends/metal_msl/artifacts/, native events at events/native-events.ndjson, FillRect image at images/fill-rect-readback.rgba, and compiler/system output at logs/system.log. PASS requires exact generated MSL compilation, positive physical device identity and handle, device-origin raw readback exactly equal to the CPU oracle, zero mismatches, and no CPU fallback. Owner: prepared-macOS evidence operator. Merge owner/final reviewer: root Codex agent at normal/highest capability.", open, true
    653, TODO, gpu, P1, "Run CUDA-to-DirectX ProcessingIR drawing translation on a native DirectX device.", test/01_unit/lib/gc_async_mut/processing/cuda_drawing_translation_spec.spl, 1, , "Linux host-independent evidence covers deterministic HLSL generation, UAV u0 and DrawParams b0 bindings, row-major py*stride+px addressing, half-open rectangle coordinates, semantic-key invalidation, and fail-closed unsupported/lossy translations; it is not DirectX execution proof. Target: Windows x86_64 with the Windows SDK D3D12 runtime and debug layer, a DirectX 12 compute-capable physical adapter (WARP is not admissible), DXC available on PATH, and an admitted source-matched pure-Simple binary. Resume exactly: SIMPLE_LIB=src bin/simple test test/03_system/app/simple_2d/feature/processing_cuda_directx_native_spec.spl --mode=interpreter. Retain generated HLSL and compiled DXIL artifacts; DXC/compiler logs, versions, diagnostics, and identities; Simple/source hashes and semantic key; physical adapter identity and feature level; backend/resource handles; D3D12 command submission, queue, fence-completion, and debug-layer event evidence; rendered output image plus dimensions/format/hash; raw device readback; CPU oracle and mismatch count; latency and max RSS under build/gpu_renderer_processing_backends/cuda_directx/. Owner: prepared-Windows evidence operator. Merge owner: root Codex agent. Final reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex reviewer.", open, true
    654, TODO, runtime, P1, "Qualify Unicode sys_get_args on native Windows.", src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/args.rs, 142, , "POSTPONED-EXTERNAL-HOST: run a native MSVC-built probe through wmain with argv0, plain text, two words, empty text, Korean, and emoji. Require exact order/content and prove the link fails when rt_set_args_wide is absent. Cross-host source and UTF-16 conversion tests are not native Windows evidence.", open, true
    655, TODO, runtime, P1, "Qualify sys_get_args on native Linux and FreeBSD.", src/runtime/simple_core/core_process.spl, 63, , "POSTPONED-PREPARED-HOSTS: run the same native probe on Linux and the canonical FreeBSD QEMU bootstrap host. Require argv0 plus plain, spaced, and empty user arguments through sys_get_args and get_cli_args, with one canonical store and no seed/fabricated provider.", open, true
    656, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Qualify sys_get_args in SimpleOS userspace under QEMU.", src/os/libc/simpleos_libc.c, 388, , "POSTPONED-QEMU: launch a userspace ELF with argv0 plus plain, spaced, and empty arguments; retain serial evidence for exact argc/order/content. Require the strong SimpleCore provider or coherent weak libc fallback and reject fabricated baremetal argv stubs.", open, true
    657, TODO, runtime, P1, "Run source-matched macOS native sys_get_args end-to-end evidence.", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/native_project/linker.rs, 759, , "POSTPONED-COMPILER-ADMISSION: after an admitted pure-Simple compiler is available, build and launch the argv probe on macOS. Require the generated main object to import rather than define rt_set_args and preserve argv0 plus plain, spaced, and empty user arguments. Rust-seed interpreter coverage is diagnostic only.", open, true
658, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Run UNO Q native board GPU pass with board-attached runner and native DrawIR parity.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-native-board-gpu-2d.shs, 1, , "The wrapper is currently fail-closed with `board-not-connected` without hardware and `live-qrb2210-simpleos-runner-required-offline-preflight-only` when attachment is asserted because this dispatcher cannot promote offline preflight into live evidence. Close TODO658 only after board-attached execution proves identity, boot/download hashes, submission/fence path, Adreno native adapter readiness, device-origin readback, and exact DrawIR/CPU-SIMD parity.", open, true
659, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Run the Simple 2D showcase evidence set on Linux QEMU, prepared macOS, and UNO Q board with Vulkan-backed DrawIR/ProcessingIR, plus animated draw + event + sound parity.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-qemu-host-gpu-2d.shs, 1, , "Open: Linux QEMU/AArch64 board-host coverage, prepared-macOS emulator only, and board-attached UNO Q pass are all required. Close only after native DrawIR and ProcessingIR checks prove exact event/animation/draw/sound parity against CPU or SIMD oracles, stable device identity, and complete receipts per platform.", open, true
    660, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Run the emulator-ready macOS Simple2D contract on a prepared macOS host; keep this Linux host fail-closed.", doc/06_spec/03_system/os/qemu/simpleos_2d_showcase_spec.md, 1, , "Implemented source readiness requires decoded/correlated 20-frame animation, move/down/drag/up/wheel, ordinary key down/up, distinct left/right Ctrl and Alt, font batch/atlas upload, one real audio submit/completion, capture, explicit Vulkan submit/fence/device readback, p95/RSS budgets, stable device identity, and no fallback. Linux provides static/unit evidence only and claims no native macOS PASS. Close only with a source-matched prepared-macOS receipt through shared DrawIR-to-Engine2D-to-Vulkan; Metal or a private renderer is not admissible proof.", open, true
    661, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Complete Simple2D showcase 4-lane proof with animation, event handling (mouse/keyboard/ctrl/alt), font rendering, and sound once board host is attached.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-qemu-host-gpu-2d.shs, 1, , "Linux QEMU and macOS-emulator lanes are parser/tests-only in this host. QRB2210 now has typed display/input/audio/GPU-submit/fence/device-readback ports and a shared WM -> DrawIR -> Engine2D -> Qualcomm Vulkan admission root, but no physical provider implementation or receipt is claimed. TODO661 still requires one fresh board-host run for native DrawIR/ProcessingIR event, animation, font, and sound parity plus stable device identity receipts.", open, true
    662, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Force and verify Vulkan-backed ProcessingIR execution on Linux host QEMU lanes (x86_64/aarch64/riscv64) during the 4-lane showcase run.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-qemu-host-gpu-2d.shs, 1, , "Current lane parser accepts cuda-preferred-vulkan-fallback and does not require Vulkan-only processing in live execution. TODO662 requires native runs with SIMPLEOS_HOST_GPU_PROCESSING_BACKEND=vulkan on all Linux rows, with processing receipts proving exact device-origin output and nonzero positive Vulkan backend identity.", open, true
    663, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Add explicit animation-frame progression receipts for host-gpu and RV64 font/input lanes in the final showcase evidence, then prove them live (not source-only).", test/03_system/os/qemu/simpleos_2d_showcase_spec.spl, 1, , "Parser currently checks animation hooks in source (`web_animation_dirty_due`, `animation_frame_due`) but no live-row frame counter proof is captured in this host. TODO663 requires captured frame-change/witness lines tied to DrawIR input sequences and parity markers before live PASS.", open, true
    664, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Close the Simple2D 4-lane session only after one attached UNO Q board run provides native DrawIR+ProcessingIR exactness, event/input parity, font, sound, and frame-progress receipts while Linux/Mac lanes remain policy-compliant and fail-closed where unsupported.", scripts/check/check-simpleos-qemu-host-gpu-2d.shs, 1, , "The QRB2210 six-provider interface and fail-closed shared composition-root admission are implemented, but every canonical capability remains PORT_UNAVAILABLE and no board execution exists. Keep the final gate blocked on real display/input/audio/Adreno submit/fence/readback providers, fresh attached hardware, board-runner readiness, and captured native artifacts (identity, receipt hash, animation frames, event traces, font and audio parity).", open, true
    665, TODO, simpleos, P1, "Run live SimpleOS QEMU pre-main startup admission with a generated manifest-aware native entry and an in-guest Clang executable.", scripts/check/check-dedicated-host-startup-wiring.shs, 1, , "The generated POSIX entry and x86-64/AArch64 CRT hook order are structural-only. Do not close this item from source scans, host unit tests, a Rust seed, or synthetic receipts. Close only after a booted SimpleOS guest runs an in-guest Clang-linked artifact whose declared argv/preload reaches the SimpleOS provider, blocks a required failure before main, and records the real guest receipt.", open, true
    666, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Admit an instrumented pure-Simple Stage 3 from a fresh current-HEAD Stage 2.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 45, doc/08_tracking/bug/stage3_current_source_hir_rss_termination_2026-08-14.md, "ACTIONABLE: historical Stage 2 `e383...` and its 41,394 MiB interrupted high-water mark are diagnostic; host capacity is not a proved root cause or remedy, and Phase2 parser versus Phase3 HIR retention remains unresolved. Four disjoint three-cycle drafts were rejected and reverted without Stage3: (1) supervisor cleanup was non-total, could abandon survivors, and had soft caps; (2) the phase publisher's new runtime providers were absent from the bootstrap-main core-C capsule projection; (3) analyzer post-link temp-unlink/directory-fsync failure could leave a completed-looking final receipt; (4) the non-circular Stage2-tuple planner producer exited incomplete tuples before its canonical diagnostic, so the reason guard was not reached. M0 must repair those exact owners together with safe phase publication, hard-bounded zero-survivor process-tree supervision under the inherited outer PGID, strict analyzer/correlation, independently verified Stage2-tuple planner admission, full-bootstrap/resume parity, compatible provenance/verifier migration, and remaining early-handshake/parent-swap/PID-reuse/sequence-gap/durability reds. After M0 acceptance, a fresh session builds current-HEAD Stage2 in absent unique output `build/restart12-riscv-current-head` and runs exactly one instrumented Stage3. Retain phase/memory/process/RSS/planner receipts, source/runtime/tool snapshots, transcripts, manifests, logs, executable hashes, and interrupted/completed terminal state. No Stage3 retry is permitted in this session. Owner: compiler memory/bootstrap lanes. Merge owner: primary bootstrap owner. Final reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex.", open, true
    667, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Qualify the x86_64 Linux Stage 4 candidate, essential-tools smoke, deployment, downstream source-matched evidence, and explicit rollback.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 46, , "GATED ON TODO666; A2 NOT REACHED. After TODO666 publishes `build/bootstrap/planner-admission/restart12-riscv-current-head/admission.env` and admits instrumented Stage3 in its fresh output, run exactly `env SIMPLE_NO_STUB_FALLBACK=1 sh scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-from-scratch.sh --bootstrap-receipt=build/bootstrap/planner-admission/restart12-riscv-current-head/admission.env --resume-stage4-from-admitted=build/restart12-riscv-current-head --deploy --jobs=1`. Accept the internal essential-tools smoke exactly once and retain `stage4-essential-tools-smoke.log`; do not run a standalone duplicate. Keep that candidate deployed while B-F/Q run, then execute rollback, unless one immutable bundle binds candidate, deploy receipt, pre-deploy binary, downstream receipts, rollback evidence, and all hashes. Owner: x86 Stage 4 admission owner. Merge owner: primary bootstrap owner. Final reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex.", blocked, true
    668, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Qualify native Linux AArch64 full bootstrap acceptance.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 51, , "BLOCKED: Exact canonical command on a native AArch64 Linux host: `sh scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-from-scratch.sh --backend=llvm --mode=dynload --full-bootstrap --full-cli --jobs=2`. Required artifacts/evidence: native host identity and toolchain versions, `build/bootstrap/stage3/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/simple`, `build/bootstrap/full/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/simple`, hashes, logs, sanity output, source/compiler hashes, and all essential-tool markers. Owner: external-host sidecar. Frontier reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex. No false PASS: QEMU-user, cross-build, Linux x86_64, Rust-seed, stale artifact, static, or synthetic evidence cannot close native AArch64; no native receipt is currently claimed.", open, true
    669, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Qualify native macOS x86_64 and AArch64 full bootstrap acceptance on both triples.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 52, , "BLOCKED: Run the exact canonical command separately on native macOS hosts for both triples: `sh scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-from-scratch.sh --backend=llvm --mode=dynload --full-bootstrap --full-cli --jobs=2`. Required artifacts/evidence for each triple: host identity, toolchain versions, matching `build/bootstrap/stage3/<triple>/simple` and `build/bootstrap/full/<triple>/simple`, hashes, logs, sanity output, source/compiler hashes, and all essential-tool markers, with explicit triple metadata and candidate lineage. Owner: external-host sidecar. Frontier reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex. No false PASS: one architecture, Linux/cross output, emulator, Rust-seed, stale artifact, static check, or synthetic receipt cannot close the other macOS triple; neither native macOS receipt is currently claimed.", open, true
    670, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Qualify the complete FreeBSD x86_64 QEMU bootstrap.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 54, , "BLOCKED: Exact canonical command: `sh scripts/check/check-freebsd-bootstrap-qemu.shs --full --download`. Required artifacts/evidence: preflight and full receipts, FreeBSD version/architecture, base-image identity and hash, source identity, exact command transcript, VM and guest logs, guest Stage 3 artifact hash, bootstrap logs, smoke markers, and one atomic full-run provenance receipt; missing or empty guest logs fail the claim. Owner: FreeBSD sidecar. Frontier reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex. No false PASS: a preflight-only, bounded/partial run, host build, Rust-seed result, stale artifact, or synthetic guest receipt cannot close full FreeBSD QEMU; TODO530 remains the related open row and no FreeBSD PASS is currently claimed.", open, true
    671, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Qualify the SimpleOS x86_64 target bootstrap artifact.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 55, , "BLOCKED: Exact canonical command: `sh scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-from-scratch.sh --target=simpleos-x86_64 --output=build/bootstrap --jobs=2`. Required artifacts/evidence: staged target artifacts, target manifest, source/compiler/toolchain identities, hashes, exact command transcript, and build logs. Owner: SimpleOS x86 target operator. Frontier reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex. No false PASS: this is target evidence only, not a hosted full-CLI claim; source scans, cross-build metadata without target artifacts, Rust-seed output, stale artifacts, and synthetic receipts do not close it.", open, true
    672, TODO, bootstrap, P1, "Qualify the SimpleOS AArch64 attested image and its live QMP input evidence.", doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/stage4_spdev.md, 56, , "BLOCKED: Exact canonical commands, in order: `sh scripts/check/build-simpleos-arm64-desktop-engine2d-attested.shs` then `sh scripts/check/check-simpleos-arm64-qmp-input-evidence.shs`. Required artifacts/evidence: attested image, producer manifest with schema/source-entry/compiler/producer/host/kernel/disk/build-log hashes and command, retained build logs, atomic consumer evidence manifest, QMP and serial logs, pre-injection watermarks, captures, and guest/capture checksum equality. Owner: SimpleOS AArch64 sidecar. Frontier reviewer: normal/highest-capability Codex. No false PASS: image-only, QMP-disconnected, source-only, cross-build, Rust-seed, stale, or synthetic evidence cannot close the live row; image/QMP evidence does not claim hosted bootstrap. UNO Q board execution remains referenced by existing TODO658 and TODO664 and is not duplicated here.", open, true
    673, TODO, llm-caret, P1, "Deploy a provenance-qualified pure-Simple runtime with canonical SSpec colon-block parsing, then run focused Caret checks and regenerate evidence.", src/compiler/10.frontend/core/parser_stmts.spl, 239, doc/08_tracking/bug/self_hosted_sspec_describe_colon_parser_2026-08-08.md, "POSTPONED-BOOTSTRAP: the deployed self-hosted runtime rejects canonical `describe ...:` / `it ...:` although the source parser supports trailing colon block arguments. Close only after a successful source-matched bootstrap/deployment executes the focused Caret CLI/TUI/hidden checks and regenerates their SSpec/manual evidence.", blocked, true
    674, TODO, llm-caret, P1, "Execute cached offline Claude PTY and hidden-command default/alias/plain Caret cases after the qualified bootstrap.", scripts/check/check-llm-caret-tui-pty.shs, 997, doc/03_plan/agent_tasks/llm_caret_claude_cli_harden.md, "POSTPONED-BOOTSTRAP: retain the cached fixture contract and run offline-claude plus hidden default, hidden alias, disabled, and plain-mode cases only with the provenance-qualified runtime. Keep PTY receipts and fail the item on any responder, persistence, hook, or terminal-lifecycle side effect from a rejected hidden command.", blocked, true
    675, TODO, sspec-live-capture, P2, "ML live-capture (T2g) blocked: libtorch unavailable, rt_torch_available() returns false. When it returns true, write live_ml_capture_spec.spl per live_audio_capture_spec.spl", test/03_system/tools/spipe/examples/live_capture_blocker_sentinels_spec.spl, 25, , "libtorch-unavailable", open, true
